course: dictionary
lesson: 14929
title: Many meanings of regard
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «I regard him as a good friend.» Here regard means think of, so the sentence says you think of him as a good friend.
explain: «She has great regard for her teacher.» Here regard is a noun that means respect or care. Try the test: does the sentence still make sense if you put respect in place of regard? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
explain: «Give my regards to your mum.» Regards with an s means kind wishes. The word give is a clue, because you can give wishes to someone, but you cannot give a mum a regard in the same way.
explain: Some uses are formal, so look for signal words. «With regard to your question, the library opens at nine» means about your question. In a letter, «Kind regards» is a polite way to end before you write your name.
fact: Regard can be a verb or a noun.
fact: As a verb, «regard» can mean to think of someone as something, as in «I regard him as a friend».
fact: As a noun, «regard» means respect or care, as in «great regard for her teacher».
fact: «Regards» in the plural means kind wishes, as in «Give my regards to your mum».
fact: «With regard to» and «regarding» mean about, and they are often used in formal writing.
exercise: «I regard him as a good friend.» What does regard mean here? | Give him a present | Look at him very carefully through a telescope | Forget his name | *Think of him as a good friend
exercise: «She has great regard for her teacher.» What is regard in this sentence? | A kind of hat | *Respect and care | Anger | A type of teacher
exercise: «Give my regards to your mum.» What do regards mean here? | Money you owe | Rules at school | *Kind wishes | Painted pictures
test: «Regarding your homework, the due date is Friday.» What does regarding mean here? | Against | Forgetting | *About | Under
test: A letter ends with «Kind regards». What kind of ending is this? | *A polite ending | A maths answer | A rude ending | A sad story ending
exam: In maths, «regard the table as a rectangle» means: | Paint the table red | Forget the table | *Treat the table as a rectangle | Measure the table with a ruler
